  "rationale": "Classic hard-bop date at the peak of Hank Mobley's Blue Note run (recorded 1963, released May 1964). The personnel network is the story: two front lines across two sessions \u2014 Lee Morgan, Andrew Hill and John Ore on the October date; Donald Byrd, Herbie Hancock and Butch Warren on the March date \u2014 all under Philly Joe Jones. AllMusic 4 stars (Jurek: 'a very gritty and realist approach to the roots of hard bop. Highly recommended'); Penguin Guide 3.5 stars. The title track and 'Three Way Split' are Mobley originals still in the hard-bop book. Session gravity + defining-statement value: this is the Mobley the canon's Soul Station/Roll Call/Workout arc was building toward, with the added historical wrinkle that the March session's material was partly reissued on The Turnaround! (1965). Consensus via AllMusic and Penguin; no artist-concentration penalty applies (Mobley already in canon).",
